1.5 Field Plots
===============

* Menu:

* Function ax_contour expr xvar xlo xhi yvar ylo yhi::


File: ax-plots.info,  Node: Function ax_contour expr xvar xlo xhi yvar ylo yhi,  Up: Field Plots

 -- Function: ax_contour (EXPR, XVAR, XLO, XHI, YVAR, YLO, YHI)
     Filled contour plot of a 2D expression.  Use inside ‘ax_draw2d’.
     Samples f(x,y) on a grid and renders as a Plotly contour chart with
     multiple filled levels.

     Distinct from ‘implicit()’ which renders a single contour line at
     f(x,y)=0.

* Menu:

     * Examples: Examples 8.
     * Relevant Options: Relevant Options 4.
     * Examples: Examples 9.
     * Relevant Options: Relevant Options 5.
     * Examples: Examples 10.
     * Relevant Options: Relevant Options 6.


File: ax-plots.info,  Node: Examples 8,  Up: Field Plots

1.5.1 Examples
--------------

/* Basic contour plot */
ax_draw2d(ax_contour(x^2 + y^2, x, -3, 3, y, -3, 3))$

/* With colorscale and contour count */
ax_draw2d(
  ax_contour(sin(x)*cos(y), x, -%pi, %pi, y, -%pi, %pi),
  colorscale="Viridis", ncontours=20,
  title="sin(x)*cos(y)"
)$

/* Hide colorbar */
ax_draw2d(
  ax_contour(x*y, x, -2, 2, y, -2, 2),
  showscale=false
)$

